        "node",
        "/Users/brad/.cache/swarm-comparison/tools/swarm-8ce795eb8/dist/cli.js",
        "With the partial: true option (and Minimatch#match(path, true)), a path should match when it is a valid prefix of a path that the full pattern could match, including when the pattern contains **. Today patterns with a globstar wrongly report false for valid prefixes. For example minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c/**\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"a\", \"a/**\", { partial: true }), minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/**/b/c/**\", { partial: true }) and minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/**\", { partial: true }) must all return true, while minimatch(\"b/a\", \"a/**\", { partial: true }) must still return false. Existing partial behavior for patterns without ** (for example \"/a/b\" against \"/*/b/x/y/z\" is true and \"/a/b/c\" is false) and makeRe(pattern, { partial: true }) must be unchanged, and non-partial matching must not loosen: minimatch(\"/b/c/d/a\", \"/**/a/b/c\") stays false. Make the change in the ** path-walking logic in src/index.ts, not by post-processing results. The library is TypeScript built with npx tshy; tests run with npm test (tap, which requires 100% coverage).\n\nVisible acceptance check (it must pass; it is not the only criterion): npx tshy && node acceptance/visible/check.mjs\nThe project's own tests run with: npm test\nDo not modify anything under acceptance/visible/.",
